1
00:00:07,197 --> 00:00:11,206
Sit by a window and listen to
the rain. The sound is clear.

2
00:00:11,286 --> 00:00:12,787
Nothing has to light it up.

3
00:00:13,585 --> 00:00:18,699
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:24,736
The books say that luminosity is the
knowing clarity of appearing itself.

5
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,583
A sound is clear as sound.

6
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:28,621
A colour is vivid as colour.

7
00:00:28,701 --> 00:00:31,167
Nothing stands behind
them to light them up.

8
00:00:31,977 --> 00:00:36,571
A careful reader of Nāgārjuna will
stop here and ask a hard question.

9
00:00:36,651 --> 00:00:38,840
In the seventh chapter of the Middle Way,

10
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:44,641
Nāgārjuna takes apart a lamp that
lights up both itself and other things.

11
00:00:44,721 --> 00:00:49,179
Later teachers use the same move
against a mind that knows itself.

12
00:00:49,259 --> 00:00:52,331
So when we say the clarity
is the appearing itself,

13
00:00:52,411 --> 00:00:56,820
are we not bringing back the
very lamp that Nāgārjuna put out?

14
00:00:57,650 --> 00:00:59,133
The short answer is no.

15
00:00:59,213 --> 00:01:04,676
Read slowly, Nāgārjuna's lamp is the
clearest proof we have that clarity is

16
00:01:04,756 --> 00:01:09,817
never missing. And the clearest warning
against making it a light of its own.

17
00:01:10,638 --> 00:01:11,989
Start with the lamp.

18
00:01:13,197 --> 00:01:17,016
Chapter seven looks at
arising, staying and ceasing.

19
00:01:17,096 --> 00:01:21,378
The opponent wants arising to
produce both the thing and itself,

20
00:01:21,458 --> 00:01:23,959
so that no second arising is needed.

21
00:01:24,039 --> 00:01:25,657
He reaches for an image.

22
00:01:25,737 --> 00:01:29,380
Just as a lamp lights up
both itself and other things,

23
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:33,746
so arising gives rise to
both itself and other things.

24
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:36,655
Nāgārjuna looks at the lamp.

25
00:01:36,735 --> 00:01:40,622
There is no darkness in the
lamp, nor where the lamp stands.

26
00:01:40,702 --> 00:01:42,393
Then what does the lamp light up?

27
00:01:42,482 --> 00:01:45,328
For lighting up means dispelling darkness.

28
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:48,335
Then he looks at the darkness around it.

29
00:01:48,415 --> 00:01:52,248
A lamp that is just coming to
be does not reach the darkness.

30
00:01:52,328 --> 00:01:55,767
And if a lamp could dispel
darkness without reaching it,

31
00:01:55,847 --> 00:02:00,025
then a lamp standing here would dispel
the darkness of the whole world.

32
00:02:00,825 --> 00:02:02,565
And he turns the image round.

33
00:02:02,645 --> 00:02:05,731
If a lamp lights up
both itself and others,

34
00:02:05,811 --> 00:02:09,730
then darkness too would
hide both itself and others.

35
00:02:10,549 --> 00:02:13,557
None of this stops anyone
reading by lamplight.

36
00:02:13,701 --> 00:02:16,855
"The lamp lit the room"
works in daily life.

37
00:02:16,935 --> 00:02:19,966
What fails is a lamp
with a power of its own,

38
00:02:20,046 --> 00:02:25,143
which turns back on itself, or crosses
over and acts on a separate thing called

39
00:02:25,223 --> 00:02:26,423
darkness.

40
00:02:27,102 --> 00:02:30,790
The same lamp came back later,
in a debate about the mind.

41
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:36,620
Some Buddhist thinkers held that every
moment of knowing also knows itself.

42
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:38,780
Their favourite example was the lamp.

43
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,633
A lamp needs no second lamp to be seen.

44
00:02:41,713 --> 00:02:45,415
So a cognition needs no
second cognition to be known.

45
00:02:46,225 --> 00:02:50,112
The Middle Way writers answered
with Nāgārjuna's own tools.

46
00:02:50,192 --> 00:02:52,164
A sword does not cut itself.

47
00:02:52,244 --> 00:02:54,582
A fingertip does not touch itself.

48
00:02:54,662 --> 00:02:59,854
If knowing turns back to know itself,
it splits into a knower and a known.

49
00:02:59,934 --> 00:03:03,794
Shāntideva took up the lamp
and gave Nāgārjuna's answer:

50
00:03:03,874 --> 00:03:08,305
the lamp is not lit up, because
it was never hidden by darkness.

51
00:03:08,385 --> 00:03:11,267
And Nāgārjuna had already
said it of the eye.

52
00:03:11,347 --> 00:03:13,237
Seeing does not see itself.

53
00:03:13,317 --> 00:03:17,236
And if it does not see itself,
how will it see anything else?

54
00:03:18,066 --> 00:03:19,712
So the challenge is fair.

55
00:03:19,792 --> 00:03:23,081
If our clarity is a knowing
that shines on itself,

56
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:26,043
or a light that lights
up sounds and colours,

57
00:03:26,123 --> 00:03:28,833
it falls to every one of these arguments.

58
00:03:29,649 --> 00:03:32,123
Now read that verse again, slowly.

59
00:03:32,203 --> 00:03:34,383
There is no darkness in the lamp.

60
00:03:35,197 --> 00:03:38,391
Nāgārjuna does not say the lamp is dark.

61
00:03:38,471 --> 00:03:41,978
He says the opposite: there
is no darkness in it at all.

62
00:03:42,058 --> 00:03:45,307
That is why "the lamp lights
itself" describes nothing.

63
00:03:45,387 --> 00:03:47,648
There is nothing dark in it to be lit.

64
00:03:48,462 --> 00:03:50,461
Put a sound in place of the lamp.

65
00:03:50,541 --> 00:03:53,518
Is there a moment when the
sound is there but dark,

66
00:03:53,598 --> 00:03:57,649
waiting for an awareness to
light it up? Look. There is not.

67
00:03:57,729 --> 00:03:59,727
The sound is clear as it sounds.

68
00:03:59,807 --> 00:04:01,580
There is no darkness in it.

69
00:04:02,397 --> 00:04:06,434
So the verse that refutes self-lighting
also shows something else.

70
00:04:06,514 --> 00:04:08,390
Clarity is never missing.

71
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:11,067
No appearing ever waited in the dark.

72
00:04:11,147 --> 00:04:15,564
And because no appearing was ever
dark, nothing has to light it up.

73
00:04:15,644 --> 00:04:18,109
Not another light, and not itself.

74
00:04:18,913 --> 00:04:23,316
As I once put it: you cannot talk
about phenomena without clarity.

75
00:04:23,396 --> 00:04:27,057
Just whether clarity is
abstracted out and reified.

76
00:04:27,869 --> 00:04:30,316
A phenomenon is whatever can be known.

77
00:04:30,396 --> 00:04:33,808
There is no unknown phenomenon
sitting in the dark,

78
00:04:33,888 --> 00:04:36,665
which a knower then reaches and lights up.

79
00:04:37,473 --> 00:04:41,129
Nāgārjuna opens the Middle
Way with four corners.

80
00:04:41,209 --> 00:04:44,866
Not from itself, not from
another, not from both,

81
00:04:44,946 --> 00:04:46,713
and not without a cause.

82
00:04:46,793 --> 00:04:50,373
Put the clarity of a sound
through the same four corners.

83
00:04:51,181 --> 00:04:55,938
Lit by itself? Then the sound would
have to turn back and shine on itself,

84
00:04:56,018 --> 00:04:58,288
a second act on top of the first.

85
00:04:58,368 --> 00:05:02,120
Like the blade and the
fingertip, that act is not found.

86
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:04,651
And there was no darkness in it to lift.

87
00:05:05,465 --> 00:05:09,760
Lit by another? Then an awareness
behind the sound would have to reach it.

88
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:13,360
This is the witness, the
background, the mirror.

89
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,797
It is looked for, and not found.

90
00:05:16,591 --> 00:05:20,429
Lit by both? That only adds
the two problems together.

91
00:05:21,254 --> 00:05:23,348
Without conditions? No.

92
00:05:23,428 --> 00:05:27,479
The sound is clear only with an
ear, the sound's own conditions,

93
00:05:27,559 --> 00:05:29,449
attention and the rest.

94
00:05:29,529 --> 00:05:32,931
Block the ear, and there
is no sound to be clear.

95
00:05:33,762 --> 00:05:38,655
So what is left? The sound, clear
as it sounds, on its conditions.

96
00:05:38,735 --> 00:05:41,603
That is all "self-luminous" can mean here.

97
00:05:41,683 --> 00:05:44,389
It is a denial: not lit by another.

98
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,794
It does not say the sound lights itself.

99
00:05:46,874 --> 00:05:51,064
It says the question, what lights
it, never had a place to start.

100
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,736
Here is a test anyone can do.

101
00:05:53,816 --> 00:05:57,055
Sit in a room with the
lights off. Pitch dark.

102
00:05:57,877 --> 00:06:01,234
Is anything clear? Yes. The darkness.

103
00:06:01,314 --> 00:06:03,965
It is seen, vividly, as dark.

104
00:06:04,045 --> 00:06:05,949
You know at once that it is dark.

105
00:06:06,029 --> 00:06:09,210
Seeing darkness is not
a failure of clarity.

106
00:06:09,290 --> 00:06:12,271
It is a sight, as clear as any other.

107
00:06:13,086 --> 00:06:16,145
That is the last verse of
the lamp, turned round.

108
00:06:16,225 --> 00:06:21,842
If darkness could hide itself, we could
not even know that it is dark. But we do.

109
00:06:22,653 --> 00:06:25,046
So "luminous" does not mean bright.

110
00:06:25,126 --> 00:06:27,124
A dull ache is clear as dull.

111
00:06:27,204 --> 00:06:29,339
A faint sound is clear as faint.

112
00:06:29,419 --> 00:06:32,260
Even confusion is known as confusion.

113
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:34,996
Whatever appears is known as it appears.

114
00:06:35,809 --> 00:06:39,465
Now take the six streams: seeing, hearing,

115
00:06:39,545 --> 00:06:43,093
smelling, tasting, touching and thinking.

116
00:06:43,173 --> 00:06:45,348
Each is clear on its own conditions.

117
00:06:45,428 --> 00:06:48,976
There is no single lamp moving
from the eye to the ear,

118
00:06:49,056 --> 00:06:50,733
lighting each in turn.

119
00:06:51,546 --> 00:06:54,170
But the clarity feels
the same in all of them.

120
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:59,415
The mind notices this sameness and
lifts it out. Awareness. Presence.

121
00:06:59,495 --> 00:07:02,417
The one light in which all six appear.

122
00:07:02,497 --> 00:07:05,964
Once lifted out, it is
taken to stand on its own,

123
00:07:06,044 --> 00:07:10,801
as a background, a witness, a
Mind that gives off appearances.

124
00:07:10,881 --> 00:07:14,786
That is Nāgārjuna's lamp,
put back up on its stand.

125
00:07:15,585 --> 00:07:19,010
Left as it is, the
sameness is not lifted out.

126
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:22,475
It stays the appearing's
own. This sound's clearness.

127
00:07:22,555 --> 00:07:24,214
This colour's vividness.

128
00:07:24,294 --> 00:07:26,035
Six lamps, not one.

129
00:07:26,115 --> 00:07:28,281
And no lamp that lights itself.

130
00:07:29,101 --> 00:07:32,676
The early discourse says: luminous, monks,

131
00:07:32,756 --> 00:07:37,051
is the mind, and it is defiled
by incoming defilements.

132
00:07:37,131 --> 00:07:41,806
Read this way, the defilements are
incoming because they do not belong to the

133
00:07:41,886 --> 00:07:46,820
mind's nature. The mind has no nature
of its own for them to belong to.

134
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:48,994
Its clarity was never dark.

135
00:07:49,074 --> 00:07:50,841
That is all the line needs.

136
00:07:50,921 --> 00:07:54,446
It does not need a lamp that
is always on behind the six.

137
00:07:55,278 --> 00:07:58,255
The tantras give the
lamp its strongest form.

138
00:07:58,335 --> 00:08:04,003
In Tibetan teaching on death, the coarse
elements dissolve one into the next.

139
00:08:04,083 --> 00:08:06,842
White, red and black appearances follow.

140
00:08:06,922 --> 00:08:10,742
Then comes the clear light,
the innate mind of clear light,

141
00:08:10,822 --> 00:08:13,844
said to have no beginning and no end.

142
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:17,882
It is easy to picture this
as a lamp under a basket.

143
00:08:17,962 --> 00:08:20,342
Life piles coarse minds on top of it.

144
00:08:20,422 --> 00:08:23,263
Death lifts them off, and the true light,

145
00:08:23,343 --> 00:08:25,985
there all along, is laid bare.

146
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:30,957
The teachers themselves say it is
not a soul, and that it is empty.

147
00:08:31,037 --> 00:08:33,580
Each moment of it arises and passes.

148
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:36,406
And they say a clear
light that only shines,

149
00:08:36,486 --> 00:08:39,549
and does not see emptiness, frees nothing.

150
00:08:40,349 --> 00:08:43,317
Read with the logic, three things change.

151
00:08:44,121 --> 00:08:47,424
Subtle means fewer conditions,
not a deeper stuff.

152
00:08:47,504 --> 00:08:52,315
As the coarse winds dissolve, the
conditions that tie the knot stop arising.

153
00:08:52,395 --> 00:08:56,581
What appears is one more appearing,
clear on its own conditions.

154
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:58,855
Not a floor that was waiting underneath.

155
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,855
The coarse minds were never darkness.

156
00:09:01,935 --> 00:09:04,152
A coarse thought is clear as a thought.

157
00:09:04,232 --> 00:09:06,964
A solid table is vivid as a table.

158
00:09:07,044 --> 00:09:10,198
What the coarse minds add
is the knot, not a cover.

159
00:09:10,278 --> 00:09:12,317
So nothing is uncovered at death.

160
00:09:12,397 --> 00:09:15,012
What can happen is that
the knot does not form.

161
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:20,359
And "without beginning" is a
stream, neither carried nor cut.

162
00:09:20,439 --> 00:09:24,910
Each moment depends on the one
before, neither the same nor another.

163
00:09:24,990 --> 00:09:26,600
Nothing travels through it.

164
00:09:27,418 --> 00:09:30,857
Some practice sets out to
keep awareness unbroken,

165
00:09:30,937 --> 00:09:34,567
through the day, into
dream, through deep sleep.

166
00:09:34,647 --> 00:09:36,663
Awareness twenty-four seven.

167
00:09:37,465 --> 00:09:40,347
In whatever case, there
cannot be maintenance.

168
00:09:40,427 --> 00:09:42,213
Maintenance is the split.

169
00:09:42,302 --> 00:09:47,915
For recognition to be complete, it must
unbind the habitual tendencies of seeing

170
00:09:47,995 --> 00:09:49,613
in an inherent pattern.

171
00:09:49,693 --> 00:09:51,868
Not an effort kept up during sleep.

172
00:09:51,948 --> 00:09:56,923
The process is effortless, because
clear recognition frees one from seeing

173
00:09:57,003 --> 00:10:01,248
inherency. A wisdom practice,
rather than calm abiding.

174
00:10:02,082 --> 00:10:04,747
To keep awareness going,
there must be two.

175
00:10:04,827 --> 00:10:07,247
An awareness, and someone keeping it up.

176
00:10:07,327 --> 00:10:11,486
However fine the effort, it sets
a keeper beside what is kept.

177
00:10:11,566 --> 00:10:14,153
The very gap that anatta saw through.

178
00:10:14,961 --> 00:10:17,530
What has to go is a habit, not a gap.

179
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:20,614
The problem was never that
awareness goes out at night.

180
00:10:20,694 --> 00:10:23,807
It is the habit of tying
appearings into things,

181
00:10:23,887 --> 00:10:28,459
a self, a world out there, and
now a lasting awareness too.

182
00:10:29,269 --> 00:10:32,028
Effortless is the fruit, not the start.

183
00:10:32,108 --> 00:10:35,194
Before recognition there is work: looking,

184
00:10:35,274 --> 00:10:37,287
questioning, seeing through.

185
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:41,897
What is effortless is what comes after,
when nothing needs to be held up.

186
00:10:42,713 --> 00:10:45,078
And a caution, from experience.

187
00:10:45,158 --> 00:10:49,535
Many have suffered enormous sleeplessness
and energy imbalances from these

188
00:10:49,615 --> 00:10:53,584
practices. They have to be
guided by a qualified master.

189
00:10:53,664 --> 00:10:58,203
For the insights of anatta and
emptiness, they are not necessary.

190
00:10:58,283 --> 00:11:01,632
If sleeplessness goes
on, see a doctor as well.

191
00:11:02,445 --> 00:11:07,066
If each instant is complete,
sleep is complete as sleep.

192
00:11:07,146 --> 00:11:09,389
It needs no witness standing guard.

193
00:11:09,469 --> 00:11:13,098
A Chan master was asked whether he
still made an effort in the Way.

194
00:11:13,178 --> 00:11:15,829
He said: when hungry, I eat.

195
00:11:15,909 --> 00:11:17,569
When tired, I sleep.

196
00:11:17,649 --> 00:11:21,237
Everyone does that, said
the questioner. No, he said.

197
00:11:21,317 --> 00:11:24,145
Others will not simply eat when they eat,

198
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,033
or sleep when they sleep.

199
00:11:26,113 --> 00:11:27,736
Their minds keep running on.

200
00:11:28,550 --> 00:11:31,188
The keeper is what
stops sleep being sleep.

201
00:11:31,268 --> 00:11:35,975
Without the keeper, sleeping is
fully sleeping, and nothing is lost.

202
00:11:36,773 --> 00:11:40,185
Try it now. Close your
eyes, and let a sound come.

203
00:11:40,265 --> 00:11:42,703
A fan, a car, rain.

204
00:11:43,534 --> 00:11:46,471
Was there a moment when the
sound was there but dark,

205
00:11:46,551 --> 00:11:48,948
before awareness reached it? Look.

206
00:11:49,765 --> 00:11:52,647
Is the hearing turning
back to light itself up?

207
00:11:52,727 --> 00:11:55,803
Is there a second act on
top of the hearing? Look.

208
00:11:56,609 --> 00:12:00,360
Is there a light behind the
sound, which the sound appears in?

209
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,036
Look for where it stands.

210
00:12:02,853 --> 00:12:07,981
Then open your eyes in a dim room,
and see the dark. It is clear as dark.

211
00:12:08,785 --> 00:12:11,843
What is found is the
sound, clear as it sounds,

212
00:12:11,923 --> 00:12:16,916
and the dark, clear as it is
dark. No lamp. And no darkness.

213
00:12:17,717 --> 00:12:20,725
Clear and empty. Never a hidden substance.

